<title>EGYPT: Romanian captain asks passengers to push plane.</title>
<headline>Romanian captain asks passengers to push plane.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-11-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The captain of a BAC-111 of the Romanian airline Tarom asked his passengers to get out and push the plane away from the terminal at Cairo airport on Sunday because the plane had no towing arm, airport sources said.</p>
<p>But the passengers failed to budge it and they have gone off to an airport hotel while the airline and the airport authorities think of another solution, they said.</p>
<p>The plane was originally scheduled to take off for Bucharest at 1.40 a.m. (2340 GMT Saturday).</p>
